(7456743, 1181181, 94815, '<td valign="top">This is an amazing feat of focusing prowess. As a manual focus lens with the widest aperture of any 50mm lens, it is extremely difficult to focus quickly and accurately (as you know of course). I can only think you took zillions of shots and this is the one that worked. A dazzling accomplishment in any context.</td>', 'This is an amazing feat of focusing prowess. As a manual focus lens with the widest aperture of any 50mm lens, it is extremely difficult to focus quickly and accurately (as you know of course). I can only think you took zillions of shots and this is the one that worked. A dazzling accomplishment in any context.', '2016-05-25 22:23:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7456746, 1181312, 119012, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sarampo:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Mike:</b></div><hr/><i> you could have at least cited your inspiration.. :P<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1078939" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1792/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1078939.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1792/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1078939.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1792/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1078939.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>And I love the tones of your photo, Mike, great composition! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i was kidding, hence the " :P "<br/> <br/>congrats on the ribbon, its not an easy shot to do.</td>', 'Originally posted by sarampo: Originally posted by Mike: you could have at least cited your inspiration.. :P    And I love the tones of your photo, Mike, great composition!   i was kidding, hence the " :P " congrats on the ribbon, its not an easy shot to do.', '2016-05-25 22:27:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7456772, 1181181, 100393, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tvsometime:</b></div><hr/><i> This is an amazing feat of focusing prowess. As a manual focus lens with the widest aperture of any 50mm lens, it is extremely difficult to focus quickly and accurately (as you know of course). I can only think you took zillions of shots and this is the one that worked. A dazzling accomplishment in any context. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Absolutely right Tom - I focused on a fixed point and shot at 11fps as my wife threw the dog''s toy past me. I have a number of more engaging dog poses - completely mid air for example - where she wasn''t in the plane of focus.<br/> <br/>It''s one of the reasons I got the SL, to be able to get this sort of dynamic shot, my M240 wouldn''t have made it so achievable.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-06-16 01:36:42.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by tvsometime: This is an amazing feat of focusing prowess. As a manual focus lens with the widest aperture of any 50mm lens, it is extremely difficult to focus quickly and accurately (as you know of course). I can only think you took zillions of shots and this is the one that worked. A dazzling accomplishment in any context.   Absolutely right Tom - I focused on a fixed point and shot at 11fps as my wife threw the dog''s toy past me. I have a number of more engaging dog poses - completely mid air for example - where she wasn''t in the plane of focus. It''s one of the reasons I got the SL, to be able to get this sort of dynamic shot, my M240 wouldn''t have made it so achievable.', '2016-05-26 01:52:43.000000', '2016-06-16 02:36:42.000000', 0),
